<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks in San Diego</b><ul class="chips"><li>Wildfire</li><li>Santa Ana winds</li><li>Flash flooding</li><li>Water leaks</li><li>Tile roofs</li></ul><p class="hoods"><b>Neighborhoods we often work in:</b> Scripps Ranch, Rancho Bernardo, Clairemont, North Park, La Jolla, Southcrest</p></div>

<h2>A history of canyon fires</h2>
<p>The 2003 Cedar Fire destroyed more than two thousand homes across San Diego County, including hundreds in Scripps Ranch. Four years later, the 2007 Witch Creek Fire burned into Rancho Bernardo and other communities during a Santa Ana wind event. Those fires shaped local building codes, defensible-space rules and the way insurers price canyon-rim homes. An insurance appraiser in San Diego needs to understand both the rebuild standards and the market for fire-resistant construction.</p>
<h2>January 2024 flooding</h2>
<p>In January 2024, an intense storm dropped record rain on San Diego and flooded homes in Southcrest, Shelltown, Encanto and other southeastern neighborhoods. Many homeowners learned that flood damage from rising water isn’t covered without separate flood insurance, while roof leaks and some other water damage may be. Separating those losses is often the heart of the dispute.</p>
<h2>Housing and roofs</h2>
<p>Stucco homes with concrete or clay tile roofs are typical of Clairemont, Mira Mesa and the northern suburbs, while North Park and University Heights have Craftsman bungalows and Spanish revival homes. La Jolla and the coastal neighborhoods add high-value custom homes and condos exposed to salt air. Tile roofs dominate, and broken tile, failed underlayment and discontinued profiles are frequent sources of disagreement.</p>
<h2>Condos and water</h2>
<p>San Diego has a large stock of condominiums and townhomes, where supply-line and water heater leaks often affect several units. We read the HOA’s CC&amp;Rs and master policy alongside the owner’s unit policy to identify who should pay for what.</p>

<h2>Services available in San Diego</h2>
<p>Every California Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in San Diego and the rest of San Diego County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/policyholder-appraiser-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/home-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/commercial-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/roof-damage-appraisal/">Roof Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/santa-ana-wind-damage-appraisal/">Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/atmospheric-river-storm-claim-appraisal/">Atmospheric River &amp; Storm Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/disputed-claim-services/water-leak-claim-appraisal/">Water Leak Claim Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from San Diego property owners</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary>Was my January 2024 flood damage covered?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Damage from rising surface water generally isn’t covered without flood insurance. Roof leaks and other non-flood water damage may be. We can help separate them.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you handle tile roof disputes in San Diego?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes. Tile roof scope, underlayment and matching are among the most common issues we see in the county.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you inspect in North County?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes. We inspect throughout San Diego County, from Oceanside and Escondido to Chula Vista and the backcountry.</p></div></details></div>
